    "field": "Decadal climate prediction",
    "problem": "Making credible decadal predictions for major climate shifts like the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation (IPO) phase transition is challenging, as previous attempts often lacked a robust, process-based physical mechanism to support the forecast and its implications for global warming rates.",
    "method": "This study uses an initialized decadal climate model to predict a transition to the positive Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation phase, based on a mechanism where decadal heat content buildup in the off-equatorial western Pacific provides the conditions for an El Ni\u00f1o event to trigger the shift.",
    "task": "The task is to use an initialized decadal prediction model to forecast a transition of the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation (IPO) to a positive phase and the associated resumption of a higher rate of global warming.",
    "model": [
        "CCSM4",
        "CMIP5"
